#: rc.cpp:1
msgid "LayoutConfigWidget"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:2
msgid ""
"<h1>Keyboard Layout</h1>"
" Here you can choose your keyboard layout and model. The 'model' refers to "
"the type of keyboard that is connected to your computer, while the keyboard "
"layout defines \"which key does what\" and may be different for different "
"countries."
"<p>In addition to the 'Primary Layout', which will be used as the default, "
"you can specify additional layouts, which you can easily switch between "
"using the KDE panel.\n"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:3 rc.cpp:14 rc.cpp:24
msgid "Layout"
msgstr "Тугмалар тартиби"

#: rc.cpp:4
msgid "&Enable keyboard layouts"
msgstr "Тугмалар тарт&ибини ёқиш"

#: rc.cpp:5 rc.cpp:44 rc.cpp:67
msgid "Alt+E"
msgstr "Alt+И"

#: rc.cpp:7
msgid "Available layouts:"
msgstr "Мавжуд тугмалар тартиби:"

#: rc.cpp:8
msgid "Active layouts:"
msgstr "Актив тугмалар тартиби:"

#: rc.cpp:9
msgid "Keyboard &model:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:10
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a keyboard model. This setting is independent of your "
"keyboard layout and refers to the \"hardware\" model, i.e. the way your "
"keyboard is manufactured. Modern keyboards that come with your computer "
"usually have two extra keys and are referred to as \"104-key\" models, which "
"is probably what you want if you don't know what kind of keyboard you have.\n"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:11
msgid "Include latin layout"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:12
msgid ""
"If after you switch to this layout some keyboard shortcuts based on latin "
"keys do not work try to enable this option."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:15 rc.cpp:25
msgid "Keymap"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:16
msgid ""
"If more than one layout is present in this list, the KDE panel will offer a "
"docked flag. By clicking on this flag you can easily switch between layouts."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:17
msgid "Layout variant:"
msgstr "Тугмалар тартибининг варианти:"

#: rc.cpp:18
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a variant of your primary keyboard layout. Layout "
"variants usually represent different key maps for the same language. For "
"example, Ukrainian layout might have four variants: basic, winkeys (as in "
"Windows), typewriter (as in typewriters) and phonetic (each Ukrainian letter "
"is placed on a transliterated latin one).\n"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:19
msgid "Add >>"
msgstr "Қўшиш >>"

#: rc.cpp:20
msgid "<< Remove"
msgstr "<< Олиб ташлаш"

#: rc.cpp:26
msgid ""
"This is the list of available keyboard layouts in your system. You can add "
"layout to the active list by selecting it and pressing \"Add\" button."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:27 rc.cpp:49
msgid "Command:"
msgstr "Буйруқ:"

#: rc.cpp:28
msgid ""
"This is the command which is executed when switching to the selected layout. "
"It may help you if you want to debug layout switching, or if you want to "
"switch layouts without the help of KDE."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:29
msgid "Switching Options"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:31
msgid "Show indicator for single layout"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:32
msgid "Switching Policy"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:33
msgid ""
"If you select \"Application\" or \"Window\" switching policy, changing the "
"keyboard layout will only affect the current application or window."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:34
msgid "&Global"
msgstr "&Умумий"

#: rc.cpp:35 rc.cpp:56
msgid "Alt+G"
msgstr "Alt+З"

#: rc.cpp:36
msgid "Application"
msgstr "Дастур"

#: rc.cpp:37
msgid "&Window"
msgstr "&Ойна"

#: rc.cpp:38
msgid "Sticky Switching"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:39
msgid "Enable sticky switching"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:40
msgid ""
"If you have more than two layouts and turn this option on, switching with "
"the keyboard shortcut or clicking on the kxkb indicator will only cycle "
"through the last few layouts. You can specify the number of layouts to "
"rotate below. You can still access all layouts by right-clicking on the kxkb "
"indicator."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:41
msgid "Number of layouts to rotate:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:42 rc.cpp:45
msgid "Xkb Options"
msgstr "Xkb параметрлари"

#: rc.cpp:43
msgid "&Enable xkb options"
msgstr "Xkb параметрла&рини ёқиш"

#: rc.cpp:46
msgid ""
"Here you can set xkb extension options instead of, or in addition to, "
"specifying them in the X11 configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:47
msgid "&Reset old options"
msgstr "&Эски параметрларни тиклаш"

#: rc.cpp:48
msgid "Alt+R"
msgstr "Alt+Э"

#: rc.cpp:51
msgid "NumLock on KDE Startup"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:52
msgid ""
"If supported, this option allows you to setup the state of NumLock after KDE "
"startup."
"<p>"
"You can configure NumLock to be turned on or off, or configure KDE not to "
"set NumLock state."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:53
msgid "Turn o&ff"
msgstr "Ў&чириш"

#: rc.cpp:54
msgid "Alt+F"
msgstr "Alt+Ч"

#: rc.cpp:55
msgid "Leave unchan&ged"
msgstr "Ў&згартирмаш"

#: rc.cpp:57
msgid "T&urn on"
msgstr "Ёқ&иш"

#: rc.cpp:58
msgid "Alt+U"
msgstr "Alt+И"

#: rc.cpp:59
msgid "Keyboard Repeat"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:60
msgid "&Delay:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:61
msgid " msec"
msgstr " мс"

#: rc.cpp:62
msgid ""
"If supported, this option allows you to set the delay after which a pressed "
"key will start generating keycodes. The 'Repeat rate' option controls the "
"frequency of these keycodes."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:63
msgid "&Rate:"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:64
msgid "/s"
msgstr "/s"

#: rc.cpp:65
msgid ""
"If supported, this option allows you to set the rate at which keycodes are "
"generated while a key is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:66
msgid "&Enable keyboard repeat"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:68
msgid ""
"If you check this option, pressing and holding down a key emits the same "
"character over and over again. For example, pressing and holding down the "
"Tab key will have the same effect as that of pressing that key several times "
"in succession: Tab characters continue to be emitted until you release the "
"key."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:69
#, c-format
msgid "%"
msgstr "%"

#: rc.cpp:70 rc.cpp:72
msgid ""
"If supported, this option allows you to hear audible clicks from your "
"computer's speakers when you press the keys on your keyboard. This might be "
"useful if your keyboard does not have mechanical keys, or if the sound that "
"the keys make is very soft."
"<p>You can change the loudness of the key click feedback by dragging the "
"slider button or by clicking the up/down arrows on the spin box. Setting the "
"volume to 0% turns off the key click."
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:71
msgid "Key click &volume:"
msgstr ""

